Sure, here's an example implementation of an SSML parser in Python using the `lxml` library:
```python
from lxml import etree

class SSMLParser:
    def __init__(self):
        self._parser = etree.XMLParser(remove_blank_text=True)
        self._root = None

    def parse(self, ssml: str):
        self._root = etree.fromstring(ssml, self._parser)
        return self._root

    def _get_text(self, node):
        return node.text.strip() if node.text else ""

    def _process_speak(self, node):
        output = ""
        for child in node:
            if child.tag == "s":
                output += self._process_speak(child)
            elif child.tag == "break":
                output += f"[BREAK {child.attrib.get('time', 'medium')}]"
            elif child.tag == "emphasis":
                output += f"[EMPHASIS level='{child.attrib.get('level', 'moderate')}']{self._get_text(child)}[/EMPHASIS]"
            elif child.tag == "say-as":
                output += f"[SAY_AS interpret-as='{child.attrib.get('interpret-as')}' format='{child.attrib.get('format')}']{self._get_text(child)}[/SAY_AS]"
            elif child.tag == "prosody":
                output += f"[PROSODY rate='{child.attrib.get('rate')}' pitch='{child.attrib.get('pitch')}' volume='{child.attrib.get('volume')}']{self._get_text(child)}[/PROSODY]"
            elif child.tag == "phoneme":
                output += f"[PHONEME alphabet='{child.attrib.get('alphabet')}' ph='{self._get_text(child)}']"
            else:
                output += self._get_text(child)
        return output

    def to_text(self):
        return self._process_speak(self._root)
```
This parser has a `parse` method that takes an SSML string and returns an XML element object representing the parsed document. It also has a `to_text` method that processes the `<speak>` element and its children to generate a plain text output.

The `parse` method uses the `etree.fromstring` method to parse the SSML string into an XML element object, with the `remove_blank_text=True` option to remove any unnecessary whitespace.

The `to_text` method recursively processes each child of the `<speak>` element, handling the different SSML elements and generating the corresponding plain text output. For example, the `<break>` element is translated to a `[BREAK]` tag with an optional `time` attribute, the `<emphasis>` element is translated to an `[EMPHASIS]` tag with an optional `level` attribute, and so on.

Note that this parser is just an example and may not handle all possible SSML elements and attributes. You may need to modify it or add more code to handle additional elements or attributes as needed.

Here's an example of a C# socket client that connects to a server with IP address 192.168.0.201, sends a byte "0x01" every 10 seconds, and receives "0x01" as a health check:
```
using System;
using System.Net;
using System.Net.Sockets;
using System.Threading;

class SocketClient
{
    private Socket _clientSocket;
    private byte[] _receivedData;

    public SocketClient()
    {
        // Connect to the server
        _clientSocket = new Socket(AddressFamily.InterNetwork, SocketType.Stream, ProtocolType.Tcp);
        _clientSocket.Connect(new IPEndPoint(IPAddress.Parse("192.168.0.201"), 80));

        // Start receiving data
        _receivedData = new byte[1024];
        _clientSocket.BeginReceive(_receivedData, 0, _receivedData.Length, SocketFlags.None, new AsyncCallback(ReceiveData), null);
    }

    private void ReceiveData(IAsyncResult result)
    {
        int received = _clientSocket.EndReceive(result);
        byte[] data = new byte[received];
        Array.Copy(_receivedData, data, received);

        // Check for health check
        if (data[0] == 0x01)
        {
            Console.WriteLine("Health check received.");
        }

        // Start receiving again
        _clientSocket.BeginReceive(_receivedData, 0, _receivedData.Length, SocketFlags.None, new AsyncCallback(ReceiveData), null);
    }

    public void SendData()
    {
        while (true)
        {
            // Send "0x01" every 10 seconds
            _clientSocket.Send(new byte[] { 0x01 });
            Thread.Sleep(10000);
        }
    }
}
```
You can run the client by creating an instance of the class and calling the SendData method on it.
```
SocketClient client = new SocketClient();
client.SendData();
```
Please note that this is just an example code, there might be some issues on production environment, such as socket timeout, connection lost, threading issues, etc.

