Here is an example of a React function component that trims wallet addresses using Chakra UI:
```
import { Text } from '@chakra-ui/core';

const TrimmedAddress = ({ address, numToTrim = 4, prefix = '', suffix = '' }) => {
  const trimmedAddress = `${prefix}${address.substring(0, numToTrim)}...${address.substring(address.length - numToTrim)}${suffix}`;
  return <Text>{trimmedAddress}</Text>;
};
```
This component accepts the following props:

* `address`: The wallet address to be trimmed. This is a required prop.
* `numToTrim`: The number of characters to trim from the start and end of the wallet address. This is an optional prop with a default value of `4`.
* `prefix`: A string to be added to the start of the trimmed wallet address. This is an optional prop with a default value of an empty string.
* `suffix`: A string to be added to the end of the trimmed wallet address. This is an optional prop with a default value of an empty string.

The component uses the `Text` component from Chakra UI to display the trimmed wallet address.

