Here is an example of a function that calculates the fibonacci sequence in Go:
```
func fibonacci(n int) int {
  if n <= 1 {
    return n
  }
  return fibonacci(n-1) + fibonacci(n-2)
}
```
To use this function, you would call it like this:
```
result := fibonacci(10)
```
This would calculate the 10th number in the fibonacci sequence, which is 55.

