To change your session name in the Vtiger API using React Native, you can make a new API request with the new session name.

First, you will need to obtain a new session name by logging in to the Vtiger API with your API credentials. You can do this using the following API request:
```bash
POST https://your-vtiger-url/webservice.php
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

operation=login&username=your_username&accessKey=your_access_key
```
This will return a response that includes a session name, which you can use in subsequent API requests.

To use the new session name in a React Native app, you can use a networking library like Axios or fetch to make the API request. Here is an example using Axios:
```javascript
import axios from 'axios';

const sessionName = 'your_session_name';

axios.post('https://your-vtiger-url/webservice.php', {
  operation: 'getchallenge',
  sessionName: sessionName,
})
.then(response => {
  const challengeToken = response.data.result.token;

  // Use the challenge token to make another API request
  axios.post('https://your-vtiger-url/webservice.php', {
    operation: 'login',
    username: 'your_username',
    accessKey: 'your_access_key',
    challenge: challengeToken
  })
  .then(response => {
    // Update the session name with the new value
    const newSessionName = response.data.result.sessionName;
    console.log('New session name:', newSessionName);
  })
  .catch(error => {
    console.log(error);
  });
})
.catch(error => {
  console.log(error);
});
```
In this example, we first make a `getchallenge` request to obtain a challenge token, which we then use in a subsequent `login` request to obtain a new session name. You can replace the `console.log` statements with the appropriate logic for your app.

